theory.intro:
An **arc** is part of the circumference. A **sector** is the region enclosed by two radii and the arc joining them, and the arc is the fraction $\frac{\theta}{360}$ of the whole circumference, where $\theta$ is the angle at the centre.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (0:2.6);
\coordinate (B) at (70:2.6);
\draw (O) -- (A) node[midway,below] {$r$};
\draw (O) -- (B) node[midway,above left] {$r$};
\draw[very thick] (A) arc[start angle=0,end angle=70,radius=2.6];
\pic[draw,"$\theta$",angle radius=0.75cm,angle eccentricity=2] {angle=A--O--B};
\node at (35:3.05) {$l$};
\fill (O) circle (1.6pt);
\node[below left] at (O) {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
The diagram shows a sector with centre $O$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (0:2.5);
\coordinate (B) at (70:2.5);
\draw (O) -- (A) node[midway,below] {$r$};
\draw (O) -- (B);
\draw (A) arc[start angle=0,end angle=70,radius=2.5];
\node[below left] at (O) {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Explain the difference between the **arc length** of this sector and the **perimeter** of this sector.

foundation.solution_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (0:2.5);
\coordinate (B) at (70:2.5);
\draw (O) -- (A) node[midway,below] {$r$};
\draw (O) -- (B) node[midway,above left] {$r$};
\draw[very thick] (A) arc[start angle=0,end angle=70,radius=2.5];
\node at (35:3.05) {$l$};
\node[below left] at (O) {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The arc length is the curved edge only, marked $l$.
The perimeter is the whole boundary of the sector, so it also includes the two radii.
$P = l + 2r$

